<title>UK: CRA executive heads World Coal Institute.</title>
<headline>CRA executive heads World Coal Institute.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The World Coal Institute (WCI) said on Thursday it had appointed David Klingner, group executive of Australian coal producer CRA Ltd, as its chairman.</p>
<p>The institute, a non-profit-making association of coal- producing enterprises, said in a statement that Ron Knapp, deputy director of the Minerals Council of Australia, would take over as WCI chief executive, replacing Alex Toohey.</p>
<p>Klingner took up his post on September 28. He succeeds Bob Flew, who has moved to BHP Copper, a unit of Australian resources group The Broken Hill Proprietary Company, as senior vice-president, a U.S.-based post.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom 44 171 542 7646</p>
